{
 "recipe": {
  "title": "Coin run: game rules as data, proven headless",
  "summary": "A one-room game whose whole logic is data: collect 3 coins, then reach the exit to win; the exit stays locked without them and a trap zone sends you back to the start. `checks.sim` proves each behaviour by playing scripted players through the real authoritative simulation - no window, no Rust.",
  "teaches": [
   "`vars` + `rules`: when/who/if/once/do (enter a volume, add to a variable, hide an object, emit an event, end the match)",
   "volumes from an object (`{object, pad}`), a zone (`{zone}`) or a box",
   "`teleport` to a spawn point; conditional rules with expressions (`score >= 3`)",
   "`checks.sim` scenarios: scripted walk paths + expectations on events, variables and where players end up",
   "`red_engine2 sim coin_run.json --trace out/run.json` then `replay out/run.json` for deterministic reproduction"
  ],
  "tips": [
   "Declare every variable in `vars`: a typo in a rule is a validate error, not a rule that never fires.",
   "An `emit` name that nothing listens for is fine; a `when: {event}` nothing emits is an error.",
   "Rules only run in the simulation (server / `sim`); hiding an object is state that a renderer or client acts on."
  ]
 },
